e  syrian society is very  willing to use vaccines  so they have been very the addition  the the cooperation from the people  to the vaccine campaign has been great  and  we have already over a thousand  population vaccinated  what about the fact that case numbers  are still rising despite  the vaccine drive being so successful  well they kind of overlapped so the  vaccine campaign started really  massively early february  and the numbers were rising already in  february  is a post-holiday effect that was seen  also in europe and  the us we have our  summer break from january and february  and early march so the rise  of the numbers come are probably due  to the holiday period the same  the holy season kind of the same  situation  that was uh has been observed in europe  and in  the us let me just ask  does it have anything to do with reports  that the chinese vaccine  is less effective  well there is data from  several clinical studies showing that  the cyanobacter vaccine  has efficiency  78 for the um  um cbm mild cases and  and about about 100 for the severe cases  and 50  for the very mild cases so we expect  these vaccines first to  start showing effect on the  hospitalization rates and the  under death rate um the studies in  turkey  and indonesia the efficacy data i  showed 91 and 70 and 65 percent  so the the thickness of the vaccine  based on the clinical studies  is uh between 50 and 100 depending on  the type of the case  so we expect to see that the immediately  um is able to keep the disease  uh severely reduced and how are we doing  also here  when a clinical study uh just to  check the vaccine and we have observed  so far  that about 90 percent of people show  antibodies after two weeks after the  second dose  so two weeks after the second dose we  have we see that about 90 percent of the  volunteers develop antibodies and those  antibiotics and neutralize me  okay we'll have to leave it there alexis  colleges director of the millennium  institute on